Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From Session Store to Session Store via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>32db5aed-57d1-4666-b687-b3116b4a084f</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S140caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c683a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>80</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e:41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c6:83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:27:13.3680403+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the Authenticate User Process</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Authenticate User may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to Session Store. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source process.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authentication: Use strong authentication and verify the identity of users, processes, and external services before allowing access.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From Authenticate User to Session Store via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T1840caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c683a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>81</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e:41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c6:83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:27:49.8155889+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>The Session Store Data Store Could Be Corrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across  may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to corruption of Session Store. Ensure the integrity of the data flow to the data store.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Input Validation: Validate and sanitize all inputs on the server side and use parameterized queries to prevent malicious data from being processed.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From Authenticate User to Session Store via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T18</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R840caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c683a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>82</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e:41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c6:83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:11:20.0580876+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Store Denies Session Store Potentially Writing Data</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Session Store claims that it did not write data received from an entity on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Auditing: Maintain logs containing the actor, timestamp, operation, source, and result to provide accountability and traceability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From Authenticate User to Session Store via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R8</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>I640caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c683a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>83</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e:41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c6:83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:03:43.6681275+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Sniffing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Information Disclosure</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Information disclosure happens when the information can be read by an unauthorized party.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across  may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Cryptography: Encrypt sensitive data in transit using secure TLS connections and restrict access to sensitive information.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From Authenticate User to Session Store via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>I6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D440caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c683a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>84</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e:41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c6:83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:55:47.0206945+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow  Is Potentially Interrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From Authenticate User to Session Store via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D4</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D540caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c683a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>85</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e:41a3ae7e-482c-4ecf-b22c-c55fe42759c6:83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:56:04.712037+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Store Inaccessible</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From Authenticate User to Session Store via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S283a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d2540caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d25</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>86</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464:f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d25:40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:27:17.0690763+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the Authenticate User Process</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Authenticate User may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to information disclosure by Session Store. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination process.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authentication: Use strong authentication and verify the identity of users, processes, and external services before allowing access.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From Session Store to Authenticate User via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R683a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d2540caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d25</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>87</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464:f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d25:40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:11:23.9022726+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Data Repudiation by Authenticate User</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Authenticate User claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Auditing: Maintain logs containing the actor, timestamp, operation, source, and result to provide accountability and traceability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From Session Store to Authenticate User via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D383a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d2540caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d25</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>88</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464:f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d25:40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:56:08.381154+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Process Crash or Stop for Authenticate User</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Authenticate User crashes, halts, stops or runs slowly; in all cases violating an availability metric.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From Session Store to Authenticate User via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D3</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D483a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d2540caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d25</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>89</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464:f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d25:40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:56:10.960509+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow  Is Potentially Interrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From Session Store to Authenticate User via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D4</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D583a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d2540caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d25</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>90</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464:f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d25:40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:56:12.9264055+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Store Inaccessible</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From Session Store to Authenticate User via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E683a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d2540caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d25</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>91</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464:f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d25:40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:00:07.1519431+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Authenticate User May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Session Store may be able to remotely execute code for Authenticate User.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authorization: Enforce least privilege and verify service identities so one component cannot impersonate another component.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From Session Store to Authenticate User via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E783a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d2540caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d25</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>92</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464:f0f15648-3218-4ca5-a054-2a7642e98d25:40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:00:12.0873759+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in Authenticate User</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An attacker may pass data into Authenticate User in order to change the flow of program execution within Authenticate User to the attacker's choosing.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authorization: Enforce least privilege and verify service identities so one component cannot impersonate another component.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>From Session Store to Authenticate User via unnamed</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83a3a3e9-9832-4c60-8a57-5b1ee8f5a464</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>40caa359-8109-450e-aef8-606d1b91ce7e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S250cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c24e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c364253764c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>93</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2:4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537:64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:27:19.985187+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the Checkout Service Process</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Checkout Service may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to information disclosure by Customer. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination process.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authentication: Use strong authentication and verify the identity of users, processes, and external services before allowing access.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Shipping address+ cart contents</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T150cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c24e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c364253764c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>94</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2:4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537:64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:27:51.3332927+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Lack of Input Validation for Checkout Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across Shipping address+ cart contents may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to a denial of service attack against Checkout Service or an elevation of privilege attack against Checkout Service or an information disclosure by Checkout Service. Failure to verify that input is as expected is a root cause of a very large number of exploitable issues. Consider all paths and the way they handle data. Verify that all input is verified for correctness using an approved list input validation approach.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Input Validation: Validate and sanitize all inputs on the server side and use parameterized queries to prevent malicious data from being processed.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Shipping address+ cart contents</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R650cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c24e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c364253764c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>95</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2:4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537:64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:11:28.194893+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Data Repudiation by Checkout Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Checkout Service claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Auditing: Maintain logs containing the actor, timestamp, operation, source, and result to provide accountability and traceability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Shipping address+ cart contents</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>I650cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c24e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c364253764c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>96</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2:4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537:64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:03:48.1569267+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Sniffing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Information Disclosure</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Information disclosure happens when the information can be read by an unauthorized party.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across Shipping address+ cart contents may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Cryptography: Encrypt sensitive data in transit using secure TLS connections and restrict access to sensitive information.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Shipping address+ cart contents</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>I6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D350cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c24e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c364253764c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>97</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2:4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537:64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:56:14.6396934+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Process Crash or Stop for Checkout Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Checkout Service crashes, halts, stops or runs slowly; in all cases violating an availability metric.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Shipping address+ cart contents</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D3</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D450cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c24e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c364253764c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>98</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2:4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537:64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:56:34.2259162+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Shipping address+ cart contents Is Potentially Interrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Shipping address+ cart contents</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D4</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E650cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c24e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c364253764c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>99</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2:4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537:64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:00:16.3634165+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Checkout Service May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Customer may be able to remotely execute code for Checkout Service.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authorization: Enforce least privilege and verify service identities so one component cannot impersonate another component.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Shipping address+ cart contents</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E750cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c24e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c364253764c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>100</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2:4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537:64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:00:20.4868662+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in Checkout Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An attacker may pass data into Checkout Service in order to change the flow of program execution within Checkout Service to the attacker's choosing.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authorization: Enforce least privilege and verify service identities so one component cannot impersonate another component.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Shipping address+ cart contents</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>8404dcf5-bdd8-4902-abc2-3b6c967b026150cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c24e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c364253764c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>101</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2:4e58e36f-4f91-4e09-80d9-0612c3642537:64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:00:30.8882443+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Cross Site Request Forgery</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Cross-site request forgery (CSRF or XSRF) is a type of attack in which an attacker forces a user's browser to make a forged request to a vulnerable site by exploiting an existing trust relationship between the browser and the vulnerable web site.  In a simple scenario, a user is logged in to web site A using a cookie as a credential.  The other browses to web site B.  Web site B returns a page with a hidden form that posts to web site A.  Since the browser will carry the user's cookie to web site A, web site B now can take any action on web site A, for example, adding an admin to an account.  The attack can be used to exploit any requests that the browser automatically authenticates, e.g. by session cookie, integrated authentication, IP whitelisting. The attack can be carried out in many ways such as by luring the victim to a site under control of the attacker, getting the user to click a link in a phishing email, or hacking a reputable web site that the victim will visit. The issue can only be resolved on the server side by requiring that all authenticated state-changing requests include an additional piece of secret payload (canary or CSRF token) which is known only to the legitimate web site and the browser and which is protected in transit through SSL/TLS. See the Forgery Protection property on the flow stencil for a list of mitigations.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authorization: Enforce least privilege and verify service identities so one component cannot impersonate another component.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Shipping address+ cart contents</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>50cd5546-6c33-4ed7-9148-5cef398345c2</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>8404dcf5-bdd8-4902-abc2-3b6c967b0261</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S1e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf3837aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>7aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>102</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf383:7aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038:d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:27:22.5480623+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the Update Inventory Process</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Update Inventory may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to Product/ Inventory DB. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source process.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authentication: Use strong authentication and verify the identity of users, processes, and external services before allowing access.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Decrement stock</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf383</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T18e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf3837aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>7aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>103</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf383:7aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038:d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:27:53.3928606+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>The Product/ Inventory DB Data Store Could Be Corrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across Decrement stock may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to corruption of Product/ Inventory DB. Ensure the integrity of the data flow to the data store.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Input Validation: Validate and sanitize all inputs on the server side and use parameterized queries to prevent malicious data from being processed.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Decrement stock</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf383</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T18</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R8e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf3837aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>7aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>104</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf383:7aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038:d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:11:33.7250088+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Store Denies Product/ Inventory DB Potentially Writing Data</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Product/ Inventory DB claims that it did not write data received from an entity on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Auditing: Maintain logs containing the actor, timestamp, operation, source, and result to provide accountability and traceability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Decrement stock</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf383</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R8</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>I6e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf3837aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>7aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>105</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf383:7aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038:d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:03:53.627181+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Sniffing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Information Disclosure</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Information disclosure happens when the information can be read by an unauthorized party.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across Decrement stock may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Cryptography: Encrypt sensitive data in transit using secure TLS connections and restrict access to sensitive information.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Decrement stock</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf383</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>I6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D4e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf3837aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>7aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>106</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf383:7aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038:d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:56:38.7938836+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Decrement stock Is Potentially Interrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Decrement stock</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf383</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D4</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D5e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf3837aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>7aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>107</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf383:7aabdf37-cb4a-4c7b-9136-af07b98cf038:d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:56:41.2237375+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Store Inaccessible</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Decrement stock</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>e9c11a54-c0fc-4e57-b5c2-03c439fbf383</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>d7f50881-c0ba-44f9-9c50-b2208f5f087a</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S8c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd3463b7bf39-924c-476b-b131-d847b31058b34d17f552-e6aa-41c1-830e-423b04572919</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>63b7bf39-924c-476b-b131-d847b31058b3</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>108</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34:63b7bf39-924c-476b-b131-d847b31058b3:4d17f552-e6aa-41c1-830e-423b04572919</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:27:24.1278394+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing of the Email Service Provider External Destination Entity</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Email Service Provider may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being sent to the attacker's target instead of Email Service Provider. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authentication: Use strong authentication and verify the identity of users, processes, and external services before allowing access.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Email request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>4d17f552-e6aa-41c1-830e-423b04572919</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S8</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R7c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd3463b7bf39-924c-476b-b131-d847b31058b34d17f552-e6aa-41c1-830e-423b04572919</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>63b7bf39-924c-476b-b131-d847b31058b3</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>109</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34:63b7bf39-924c-476b-b131-d847b31058b3:4d17f552-e6aa-41c1-830e-423b04572919</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:12:08.8475365+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>External Entity Email Service Provider Potentially Denies Receiving Data</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Email Service Provider claims that it did not receive data from a process on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Auditing: Maintain logs containing the actor, timestamp, operation, source, and result to provide accountability and traceability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Email request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>4d17f552-e6aa-41c1-830e-423b04572919</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D4c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd3463b7bf39-924c-476b-b131-d847b31058b34d17f552-e6aa-41c1-830e-423b04572919</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>63b7bf39-924c-476b-b131-d847b31058b3</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>110</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34:63b7bf39-924c-476b-b131-d847b31058b3:4d17f552-e6aa-41c1-830e-423b04572919</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:56:43.2913182+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Email request Is Potentially Interrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Email request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>4d17f552-e6aa-41c1-830e-423b04572919</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D4</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S2c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642fcb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>111</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8:e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f:cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:27:25.7483066+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the Admin Order Management Process</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Admin Order Management may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to information disclosure by Admin. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination process.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authentication: Use strong authentication and verify the identity of users, processes, and external services before allowing access.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin credentials</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T1c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642fcb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>112</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8:e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f:cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:28:26.8037262+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Lack of Input Validation for Admin Order Management</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across Admin credentials may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to a denial of service attack against Admin Order Management or an elevation of privilege attack against Admin Order Management or an information disclosure by Admin Order Management. Failure to verify that input is as expected is a root cause of a very large number of exploitable issues. Consider all paths and the way they handle data. Verify that all input is verified for correctness using an approved list input validation approach.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Input Validation: Validate and sanitize all inputs on the server side and use parameterized queries to prevent malicious data from being processed.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin credentials</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R6c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642fcb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>113</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8:e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f:cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:12:23.4153227+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Data Repudiation by Admin Order Management</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Admin Order Management claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Auditing: Maintain logs containing the actor, timestamp, operation, source, and result to provide accountability and traceability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin credentials</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>I6c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642fcb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>114</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8:e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f:cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:04:00.0588118+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Sniffing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Information Disclosure</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Information disclosure happens when the information can be read by an unauthorized party.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across Admin credentials may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Cryptography: Encrypt sensitive data in transit using secure TLS connections and restrict access to sensitive information.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin credentials</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>I6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D3c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642fcb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>115</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8:e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f:cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:56:46.1720749+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Process Crash or Stop for Admin Order Management</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Admin Order Management crashes, halts, stops or runs slowly; in all cases violating an availability metric.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin credentials</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D3</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D4c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642fcb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>116</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8:e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f:cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:56:49.4545441+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Admin credentials Is Potentially Interrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin credentials</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D4</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E6c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642fcb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>117</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8:e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f:cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:00:40.611456+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Admin Order Management May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Admin may be able to remotely execute code for Admin Order Management.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authorization: Enforce least privilege and verify service identities so one component cannot impersonate another component.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin credentials</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E7c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642fcb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>118</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8:e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f:cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:00:51.5082057+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in Admin Order Management</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An attacker may pass data into Admin Order Management in order to change the flow of program execution within Admin Order Management to the attacker's choosing.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authorization: Enforce least privilege and verify service identities so one component cannot impersonate another component.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin credentials</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>8404dcf5-bdd8-4902-abc2-3b6c967b0261c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642fcb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>119</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8:e049ccc3-6a0e-41ac-80ad-a14adff6642f:cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:00:57.1646225+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Cross Site Request Forgery</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Cross-site request forgery (CSRF or XSRF) is a type of attack in which an attacker forces a user's browser to make a forged request to a vulnerable site by exploiting an existing trust relationship between the browser and the vulnerable web site.  In a simple scenario, a user is logged in to web site A using a cookie as a credential.  The other browses to web site B.  Web site B returns a page with a hidden form that posts to web site A.  Since the browser will carry the user's cookie to web site A, web site B now can take any action on web site A, for example, adding an admin to an account.  The attack can be used to exploit any requests that the browser automatically authenticates, e.g. by session cookie, integrated authentication, IP whitelisting. The attack can be carried out in many ways such as by luring the victim to a site under control of the attacker, getting the user to click a link in a phishing email, or hacking a reputable web site that the victim will visit. The issue can only be resolved on the server side by requiring that all authenticated state-changing requests include an additional piece of secret payload (canary or CSRF token) which is known only to the legitimate web site and the browser and which is protected in transit through SSL/TLS. See the Forgery Protection property on the flow stencil for a list of mitigations.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authorization: Enforce least privilege and verify service identities so one component cannot impersonate another component.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin credentials</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>c373200b-c403-4115-bbb5-714836972bb8</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>8404dcf5-bdd8-4902-abc2-3b6c967b0261</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S1cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>120</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca:9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710:226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:27:28.8661078+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the Admin Order Management Process</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Admin Order Management may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to Orders DB. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source process.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authentication: Use strong authentication and verify the identity of users, processes, and external services before allowing access.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Orders DB</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T18cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>121</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca:9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710:226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:28:28.9233531+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>The Orders DB Data Store Could Be Corrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across Orders DB may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to corruption of Orders DB. Ensure the integrity of the data flow to the data store.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Input Validation: Validate and sanitize all inputs on the server side and use parameterized queries to prevent malicious data from being processed.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Orders DB</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T18</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R8cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>122</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca:9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710:226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:12:44.1474615+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Store Denies Orders DB Potentially Writing Data</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Orders DB claims that it did not write data received from an entity on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Auditing: Maintain logs containing the actor, timestamp, operation, source, and result to provide accountability and traceability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Orders DB</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R8</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>I6cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>123</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca:9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710:226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:06:09.0503699+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Sniffing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Information Disclosure</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Information disclosure happens when the information can be read by an unauthorized party.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across Orders DB may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Cryptography: Encrypt sensitive data in transit using secure TLS connections and restrict access to sensitive information.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Orders DB</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>I6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D4cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>124</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca:9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710:226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:57:02.4727132+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Orders DB Is Potentially Interrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Orders DB</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D4</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D5cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>125</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca:9501173e-8bf0-4878-9fe2-4823a4870710:226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:57:06.0572544+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Store Inaccessible</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Orders DB</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>cb2ae09a-fa30-4872-bf97-6894e63c14ca</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>226cea45-ce22-49e0-8f1f-7a928370d753</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D464c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8a500dfed-024f-48bb-9b84-64bb6e571101c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>a500dfed-024f-48bb-9b84-64bb6e571101</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>132</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8:a500dfed-024f-48bb-9b84-64bb6e571101:c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:57:17.759712+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Order confirmation data Is Potentially Interrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Order confirmation data</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D4</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E664c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8a500dfed-024f-48bb-9b84-64bb6e571101c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>a500dfed-024f-48bb-9b84-64bb6e571101</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>133</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8:a500dfed-024f-48bb-9b84-64bb6e571101:c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:01:01.99378+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Send Order Confirmation May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Checkout Service may be able to remotely execute code for Send Order Confirmation.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authorization: Enforce least privilege and verify service identities so one component cannot impersonate another component.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Order confirmation data</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E764c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8a500dfed-024f-48bb-9b84-64bb6e571101c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>a500dfed-024f-48bb-9b84-64bb6e571101</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>134</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8:a500dfed-024f-48bb-9b84-64bb6e571101:c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:01:13.6685915+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in Send Order Confirmation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An attacker may pass data into Send Order Confirmation in order to change the flow of program execution within Send Order Confirmation to the attacker's choosing.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authorization: Enforce least privilege and verify service identities so one component cannot impersonate another component.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Order confirmation data</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>8404dcf5-bdd8-4902-abc2-3b6c967b026164c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8a500dfed-024f-48bb-9b84-64bb6e571101c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>a500dfed-024f-48bb-9b84-64bb6e571101</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>135</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8:a500dfed-024f-48bb-9b84-64bb6e571101:c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:01:20.5584497+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Cross Site Request Forgery</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Cross-site request forgery (CSRF or XSRF) is a type of attack in which an attacker forces a user's browser to make a forged request to a vulnerable site by exploiting an existing trust relationship between the browser and the vulnerable web site.  In a simple scenario, a user is logged in to web site A using a cookie as a credential.  The other browses to web site B.  Web site B returns a page with a hidden form that posts to web site A.  Since the browser will carry the user's cookie to web site A, web site B now can take any action on web site A, for example, adding an admin to an account.  The attack can be used to exploit any requests that the browser automatically authenticates, e.g. by session cookie, integrated authentication, IP whitelisting. The attack can be carried out in many ways such as by luring the victim to a site under control of the attacker, getting the user to click a link in a phishing email, or hacking a reputable web site that the victim will visit. The issue can only be resolved on the server side by requiring that all authenticated state-changing requests include an additional piece of secret payload (canary or CSRF token) which is known only to the legitimate web site and the browser and which is protected in transit through SSL/TLS. See the Forgery Protection property on the flow stencil for a list of mitigations.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authorization: Enforce least privilege and verify service identities so one component cannot impersonate another component.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Order confirmation data</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>64c517b6-37e0-4afd-9616-acc6c156c0a8</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>c6ab27a4-2eff-4da3-9b72-5e66d69acd34</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>8404dcf5-bdd8-4902-abc2-3b6c967b0261</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R7e4304a69-66d6-45a8-8e81-4c914f626a69132e6ae1-df1b-43ea-88eb-e639d23e045383bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>132e6ae1-df1b-43ea-88eb-e639d23e0453</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>136</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>e4304a69-66d6-45a8-8e81-4c914f626a69:132e6ae1-df1b-43ea-88eb-e639d23e0453:83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:13:03.4220787+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>External Entity Payment Gateway Potentially Denies Receiving Data</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Payment Gateway claims that it did not receive data from a process on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Auditing: Maintain logs containing the actor, timestamp, operation, source, and result to provide accountability and traceability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Payment status/ Refund status</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>e4304a69-66d6-45a8-8e81-4c914f626a69</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D4e4304a69-66d6-45a8-8e81-4c914f626a69132e6ae1-df1b-43ea-88eb-e639d23e045383bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>132e6ae1-df1b-43ea-88eb-e639d23e0453</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>137</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>e4304a69-66d6-45a8-8e81-4c914f626a69:132e6ae1-df1b-43ea-88eb-e639d23e0453:83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:57:21.6144347+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Payment status/ Refund status Is Potentially Interrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Payment status/ Refund status</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>e4304a69-66d6-45a8-8e81-4c914f626a69</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D4</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D5e4304a69-66d6-45a8-8e81-4c914f626a69132e6ae1-df1b-43ea-88eb-e639d23e045383bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>132e6ae1-df1b-43ea-88eb-e639d23e0453</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>138</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>e4304a69-66d6-45a8-8e81-4c914f626a69:132e6ae1-df1b-43ea-88eb-e639d23e0453:83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:57:26.1800636+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Store Inaccessible</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Payment status/ Refund status</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>e4304a69-66d6-45a8-8e81-4c914f626a69</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S85e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c145ca32a-f105-481a-afb8-f7361e36787c83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>145ca32a-f105-481a-afb8-f7361e36787c</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>139</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c:145ca32a-f105-481a-afb8-f7361e36787c:83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:27:35.456713+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing of the Payment Gateway External Destination Entity</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Payment Gateway may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being sent to the attacker's target instead of Payment Gateway. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authentication: Use strong authentication and verify the identity of users, processes, and external services before allowing access.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Charge request/ Refund request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S8</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R75e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c145ca32a-f105-481a-afb8-f7361e36787c83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>145ca32a-f105-481a-afb8-f7361e36787c</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>140</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c:145ca32a-f105-481a-afb8-f7361e36787c:83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:13:24.5032438+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>External Entity Payment Gateway Potentially Denies Receiving Data</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Payment Gateway claims that it did not receive data from a process on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Auditing: Maintain logs containing the actor, timestamp, operation, source, and result to provide accountability and traceability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Charge request/ Refund request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D45e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c145ca32a-f105-481a-afb8-f7361e36787c83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>145ca32a-f105-481a-afb8-f7361e36787c</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>141</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c:145ca32a-f105-481a-afb8-f7361e36787c:83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:57:30.5662076+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Charge request/ Refund request Is Potentially Interrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Charge request/ Refund request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D4</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S283bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc65e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>142</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e:0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6:5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:27:40.2334568+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the Process Payment Process</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Process Payment may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to information disclosure by Payment Gateway. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination process.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authentication: Use strong authentication and verify the identity of users, processes, and external services before allowing access.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Payment result/ Refund result</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T183bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc65e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>143</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e:0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6:5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:28:32.8808419+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Lack of Input Validation for Process Payment</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across Payment result/ Refund result may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to a denial of service attack against Process Payment or an elevation of privilege attack against Process Payment or an information disclosure by Process Payment. Failure to verify that input is as expected is a root cause of a very large number of exploitable issues. Consider all paths and the way they handle data. Verify that all input is verified for correctness using an approved list input validation approach.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Input Validation: Validate and sanitize all inputs on the server side and use parameterized queries to prevent malicious data from being processed.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Payment result/ Refund result</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R683bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc65e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>144</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e:0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6:5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:13:28.0526735+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Data Repudiation by Process Payment</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Process Payment claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Auditing: Maintain logs containing the actor, timestamp, operation, source, and result to provide accountability and traceability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Payment result/ Refund result</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>I683bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc65e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>145</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e:0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6:5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:06:17.4195898+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Sniffing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Information Disclosure</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Information disclosure happens when the information can be read by an unauthorized party.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across Payment result/ Refund result may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Cryptography: Encrypt sensitive data in transit using secure TLS connections and restrict access to sensitive information.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Payment result/ Refund result</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>I6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D383bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc65e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>146</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e:0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6:5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:57:34.2298996+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Process Crash or Stop for Process Payment</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Process Payment crashes, halts, stops or runs slowly; in all cases violating an availability metric.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Payment result/ Refund result</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D3</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D483bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc65e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>147</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e:0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6:5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-12T23:57:44.3090025+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Payment result/ Refund result Is Potentially Interrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Exception Management: Apply rate limits, timeouts, resource limits, monitoring, and graceful error handling to maintain availability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Payment result/ Refund result</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D4</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E683bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc65e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>148</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e:0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6:5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:01:24.535448+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Process Payment May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Payment Gateway may be able to remotely execute code for Process Payment.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authorization: Enforce least privilege and verify service identities so one component cannot impersonate another component.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Payment result/ Refund result</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E783bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc65e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>149</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e:0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6:5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:01:28.0757496+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in Process Payment</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An attacker may pass data into Process Payment in order to change the flow of program execution within Process Payment to the attacker's choosing.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authorization: Enforce least privilege and verify service identities so one component cannot impersonate another component.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Payment result/ Refund result</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>8404dcf5-bdd8-4902-abc2-3b6c967b026183bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc65e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>150</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e:0609b789-48e4-4cb1-bfba-82942b792fc6:5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:01:35.2340961+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Cross Site Request Forgery</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Cross-site request forgery (CSRF or XSRF) is a type of attack in which an attacker forces a user's browser to make a forged request to a vulnerable site by exploiting an existing trust relationship between the browser and the vulnerable web site.  In a simple scenario, a user is logged in to web site A using a cookie as a credential.  The other browses to web site B.  Web site B returns a page with a hidden form that posts to web site A.  Since the browser will carry the user's cookie to web site A, web site B now can take any action on web site A, for example, adding an admin to an account.  The attack can be used to exploit any requests that the browser automatically authenticates, e.g. by session cookie, integrated authentication, IP whitelisting. The attack can be carried out in many ways such as by luring the victim to a site under control of the attacker, getting the user to click a link in a phishing email, or hacking a reputable web site that the victim will visit. The issue can only be resolved on the server side by requiring that all authenticated state-changing requests include an additional piece of secret payload (canary or CSRF token) which is known only to the legitimate web site and the browser and which is protected in transit through SSL/TLS. See the Forgery Protection property on the flow stencil for a list of mitigations.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authorization: Enforce least privilege and verify service identities so one component cannot impersonate another component.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Payment result/ Refund result</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>8404dcf5-bdd8-4902-abc2-3b6c967b0261</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S85e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c1ba613a6-8398-4715-b924-7f4b6d2c68ee83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>1ba613a6-8398-4715-b924-7f4b6d2c68ee</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>151</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c:1ba613a6-8398-4715-b924-7f4b6d2c68ee:83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:25:46.3297294+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing of the Payment Gateway External Destination Entity</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Payment Gateway may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being sent to the attacker's target instead of Payment Gateway. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Authentication: Use strong authentication and verify the identity of users, processes, and external services before allowing access.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Payment result/ Refund result</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S8</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R75e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c1ba613a6-8398-4715-b924-7f4b6d2c68ee83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>1ba613a6-8398-4715-b924-7f4b6d2c68ee</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>152</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c:1ba613a6-8398-4715-b924-7f4b6d2c68ee:83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-13T00:13:39.1105311+08:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>External Entity Payment Gateway Potentially Denies Receiving Data</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Payment Gateway claims that it did not receive data from a process on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key><a:Value>Auditing: Maintain logs containing the actor, timestamp, operation, source, and result to provide accountability and traceability.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Payment result/ Refund result</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>5e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c</b:SourceGuid><b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D45e9f67dc-ae06-4a78-85ec-57dc04f2878c1ba613a6-8398-4715-b924-7f4b6d2c68ee83bae77d-67e3-40ff-9015-db35e2723b5e</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy>DESKTOP-7E5D9MU\james</b:ChangedBy><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>1d9910bf-f28c-4c80-bd03-1e793bc90394</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>1ba613a6-8398-4715-b924-7f4b6d2c68ee</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>153</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>5